jbridson@kean.ucs.mun.ca writes:

> How long should you spend on a level (eg. I normally stay on level 1 
>until I have 25-30hp) ??  I almost always get blown away on level 4-6, 
>and I was wondering if I was rushing things a bit...

It sounds to me like you are spending TOO LONG on the early levels.
You should rush a bit more! The nastiness of monsters created is roughly
in proportion to your experience level, but your survivability is
90% dependent on what armor, weapons and goodies you have and only 10%
on your hit points. What goodies you have is directly proportional to
how many levels you have explored. You haven't explored many levels, so
you haven't got many goodies, but you are having to fight harder
monsters because you are getting relatively too high in XpLvl (by trying
to get your hit points up).

If there were no ghost levels, the way to win would be go as FAST as
possible through the dungeon and avoid all combat (where possible),
to keep your XpLvl low and the monsters easy while getting more goodies
because you are covering more dungeon area. Of course, if you do this
now and came across a ghost level, the monsters in the ghost level are
nasty in proportion to the previous adventurers XpLvl, not yours, so
you will very likely end up fighting soldier ants with a XpLvl 3
character, or some such thing :-(.

To sum up, you need to keep your goodies:XpLvl ratio as high as
possible. This means not hanging about on explored levels.

